            "typeClass": "compound",
            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "The dataset consists of the data used for the publication ''SOX2 is a Potential Diagnostic Biomarker and Anticancer Target in Cutaneous Squamous Cell Carcinoma in Dystrophic Epidermolysis Bullosa: A Case Series Study''. For this article mRNA expression analysis and immunohistochemistry on formalin-fixed paraffin-embedded (FFPE) tissue samples of the following groups have been conducted:\n(1): cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma (cSCC) of patients with epidermolysis bullosa  (EB-cSCC; n=9)\n(2): UV-induced cSCC of patients without EB (UV-induced cSCC; n=10) \n(3): Pseudoepitheliomatous hyperplasia in EB-patients (EB-PEHs; n=7)\n\nSpecifically, the dataset consists of the results of the differential gene expression analysis of EB-cSCC vs. UV-induced cSCC (baseline) [Folder 1] and the Pathology slide specimen images (.ndpi files) of the SOX2 immunohistochemical expression of the aforementioned three groups [Folder 2.1; 2.2; 2.3]."
                },
                "dsDescriptionDate": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionDate",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "2025-08-25"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "typeName": "subject",
            "multiple": true,
            "typeClass": "controlledVocabulary",
            "value": [
              "Medicine, Health and Life Sciences"
            ]
          },
          {
            "typeName": "keyword",
            "multiple": true,
            "typeClass": "compound",
            "value": [
              {
                "keywordValue": {
                  "typeName": "keywordValue",
